@lang en
IMPORT prelude

-- Deputies who sit on state boards in an officer's place: Gov. Code §§ 7.5, 7.6, 7.7, 7.8, 7.9 and 7.9a.
--
-- Added in pass 2 of the completion to "whole".  Pass 1 called these six sections "not applicable" as board-membership machinery; the brief has no such
-- disposition, and each of them says who may be designated, to sit where, with what powers, and who answers for the deputy's acts.  Those are encoded here.
-- The quotation lines are copied by script from the converter-made plain-text rendering of the sections (not the official text) and checked against it by srcrefs.py.
-- Target: unstable (REFUSE).  Imports: prelude only.
--
-- How the functions read.  A function named "Gov. Code § X lets ..." returns FALSE when the facts do not bring the person within what that section gives; FALSE
-- does not say that no other law gives it.  A case that the section's own words leave open is a named REFUSE.  The Constitution (Art. VII § 4, Art. IX § 2.1) is
-- not deposited, so whether a person "holds a position specified in" one of its subdivisions is a fact the caller supplies.
--
-- Fork F-7.8: § 7.8 says the Directors "may appoint ... irrespective of whether there shall be more than one such person representing a director at any meeting".
-- That is read as lifting § 7.5's limit of one director represented per meeting, at the State Allocation Board.  It could also mean that several persons may
-- represent the same director; the text does not say, and the function for that question refuses.
-- Fork F-7.6f: § 7.6(f) limits "officer[s] subject to this section" represented by "deputy[ies] subject to this section"; it is read as counting only
-- officers designating under § 7.6, so a director represented under § 7.5 or § 7.9 is not counted.

§ `Nouns of the deputy provisions`

DECLARE `Office the text names` IS ONE OF
    `the Lieutenant Governor`
    `the Chief Justice of the California Supreme Court`
    `the Attorney General`
    `the Superintendent of Public Instruction`
    `the Controller`
    `the Treasurer`
    `the Director of Finance`
    `the Director of General Services`
    `the Director of Education`
    `an office the text does not name`

DECLARE `Body at whose meeting a deputy acts` IS ONE OF
    `the Senate`
    `the Regents of the University of California`
    `the Trustees of the California State University`
    `the State Board of Education`
    `the State Lands Commission`
    `the State Allocation Board`
    `another state board, commission, committee or governing body`

DECLARE `Act of a member` IS ONE OF
    `being counted in constituting a quorum`
    `participating in the proceedings`
    `voting upon any and all matters`
    `any other act the member could do if personally present`

DECLARE `Provision that designates a deputy` IS ONE OF
    `Section 7.5`
    `Section 7.6`
    `Section 7.8`
    `Section 7.9(a)`
    `another provision`

DECLARE `Extent of an officer's responsibility` IS ONE OF
    `the same extent as for the deputy's official duties in the deputy's own post`
    `a greater extent`
    `a lesser extent`

DECLARE `Category level of a career executive` IS ONE OF
    `category level IV`
    `category level V`
    `another category level`

§ `Gov. Code § 7.5: a director of a state department`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:22 | 7.5. Whenever, by any law, the director of any state department is made a member of a state board, commission, or committee, or of the governing body of any state agency or authority, the director may designate a deputy director of that department holding a position specified in subdivision (f) or (g) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution to act as such member in his or her place and stead, to all intents and purposes as though the director were personally present, including the right of the deputy to be counted in constituting a quorum, to participate in the proceedings of the board, commission, committee, or other governing body, and to vote upon any and all matters. Not more than one director shall be represented by such a deputy at any meeting or session of a board, commission, committee, or other governing body. The director so designating such a deputy shall be responsible for the acts of the deputy acting under such designation in the same manner and to the same extent that the director is responsible for the acts of the deputy performing his or her official duties as deputy director of the department.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.5 (src:GOV-ss-1-26:22)
GIVEN `the director is by law a member of a state board, commission, or committee, or of the governing body of a state agency or authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a deputy director of that department` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds a position specified in subdivision (f) or (g) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Gov. Code § 7.5 lets the director designate` `the director is by law a member of a state board, commission, or committee, or of the governing body of a state agency or authority` `the person is a deputy director of that department` `the person holds a position specified in subdivision (f) or (g) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution` MEANS
        `the director is by law a member of a state board, commission, or committee, or of the governing body of a state agency or authority`
    AND `the person is a deputy director of that department`
    AND `the person holds a position specified in subdivision (f) or (g) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:22 | 7.5. Whenever, by any law, the director of any state department is made a member of a state board, commission, or committee, or of the governing body of any state agency or authority, the director may designate a deputy director of that department holding a position specified in subdivision (f) or (g) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution to act as such member in his or her place and stead, to all intents and purposes as though the director were personally present, including the right of the deputy to be counted in constituting a quorum, to participate in the proceedings of the board, commission, committee, or other governing body, and to vote upon any and all matters. Not more than one director shall be represented by such a deputy at any meeting or session of a board, commission, committee, or other governing body. The director so designating such a deputy shall be responsible for the acts of the deputy acting under such designation in the same manner and to the same extent that the director is responsible for the acts of the deputy performing his or her official duties as deputy director of the department.
-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:24 | 7.6. (a) If by law, any officer whose office is created by the California Constitution is made a member of a state board, commission, or committee, or of the governing body of any state agency or authority, the officer may designate a deputy of his or her office holding a position specified in subdivision (c) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution to act as the member in the constitutional officer’s place and stead, to all intents and purposes as though the constitutional officer was personally present, including the right of the deputy to be counted in constituting a quorum, to participate in the proceedings of the board, commission, committee, or other governing body, and to vote upon any and all matters. The constitutional officer so designating a deputy shall be responsible for the acts of the deputy acting under the designation in the same manner and to the same extent that the constitutional officer is responsible for the acts of the deputy performing his or her official duties as a deputy of the office of the constitutional officer.
-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:35 | 7.9. (a) Notwithstanding any provision of law to the contrary, the Controller, the Treasurer, the Director of Finance, or the Superintendent of Public Instruction may designate any deputy of his or her office to act in his or her place and stead on any state board, commission, committee, or governing board of a state agency with respect to the exercise of statutory powers and duties of any of those bodies. The deputy, while sitting on a board, commission, committee, or governing board of a state agency may exercise the same powers that the Controller, the Treasurer, the Director of Finance, or the Superintendent of Public Instruction may exercise as if he or she were personally present. The Controller, the Treasurer, the Director of Finance, or the Superintendent of Public Instruction so designating a deputy shall be responsible for the acts of the deputy acting under the designation in the same manner and to the same extent that the Controller, the Treasurer, the Director of Finance, or the Superintendent of Public Instruction is responsible for the acts of the deputy performing his or her official duties as deputy to the Controller, the Treasurer, the Director of Finance, or the Superintendent of Public Instruction.
-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:33 | 7.8. Notwithstanding anything in this code to the contrary, the Directors of Finance, General Services, and Education may appoint any deputy or assistant director in their respective departments to act in their place and stead on the State Allocation Board, irrespective of whether said deputy or assistant director holds a position specified in subdivision (g) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution, and irrespective of whether there shall be more than one such person representing a director at any meeting of such board. Such person, while sitting on said board, shall have all the powers the director he represents would have had, including the right to be counted in a quorum, the right to participate in the proceedings of the board and to vote on any and all matters. The director so designating such a deputy or assistant director shall be responsible for the acts of the person acting under such designation in the same manner and to the same extent that the director is responsible for the acts of the deputy or assistant director performing his official duties as deputy or assistant director of the department.
-- What a designated deputy may do.  §§ 7.5, 7.6(a), 7.8 and 7.9(a) each say the deputy acts in the officer's place and stead, as though the officer were personally
-- present; §§ 7.5, 7.6(a) and 7.8 list being counted for a quorum, participating, and voting, and § 7.9(a) says the deputy "may exercise the same powers".  The four
-- acts below are those words; a provision that is not one of the four is not answered.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.5, § 7.6(a), § 7.8, § 7.9(a) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:22, src:GOV-ss-1-26:24, src:GOV-ss-1-26:33, src:GOV-ss-1-26:35)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision that designates a deputy`
      `the person was designated under the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      act IS AN `Act of a member`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a designated deputy may do the act in the officer's place` provision `the person was designated under the provision` act MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF provision EQUALS `another provision`
            THEN REFUSE "Gov. Code §§ 7.5, 7.6(a), 7.8 and 7.9(a) say what a deputy designated under them may do; no other provision is deposited that does"
        OTHERWISE `the person was designated under the provision`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:22 | 7.5. Whenever, by any law, the director of any state department is made a member of a state board, commission, or committee, or of the governing body of any state agency or authority, the director may designate a deputy director of that department holding a position specified in subdivision (f) or (g) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution to act as such member in his or her place and stead, to all intents and purposes as though the director were personally present, including the right of the deputy to be counted in constituting a quorum, to participate in the proceedings of the board, commission, committee, or other governing body, and to vote upon any and all matters. Not more than one director shall be represented by such a deputy at any meeting or session of a board, commission, committee, or other governing body. The director so designating such a deputy shall be responsible for the acts of the deputy acting under such designation in the same manner and to the same extent that the director is responsible for the acts of the deputy performing his or her official duties as deputy director of the department.
-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:24 | 7.6. (a) If by law, any officer whose office is created by the California Constitution is made a member of a state board, commission, or committee, or of the governing body of any state agency or authority, the officer may designate a deputy of his or her office holding a position specified in subdivision (c) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution to act as the member in the constitutional officer’s place and stead, to all intents and purposes as though the constitutional officer was personally present, including the right of the deputy to be counted in constituting a quorum, to participate in the proceedings of the board, commission, committee, or other governing body, and to vote upon any and all matters. The constitutional officer so designating a deputy shall be responsible for the acts of the deputy acting under the designation in the same manner and to the same extent that the constitutional officer is responsible for the acts of the deputy performing his or her official duties as a deputy of the office of the constitutional officer.
-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:33 | 7.8. Notwithstanding anything in this code to the contrary, the Directors of Finance, General Services, and Education may appoint any deputy or assistant director in their respective departments to act in their place and stead on the State Allocation Board, irrespective of whether said deputy or assistant director holds a position specified in subdivision (g) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution, and irrespective of whether there shall be more than one such person representing a director at any meeting of such board. Such person, while sitting on said board, shall have all the powers the director he represents would have had, including the right to be counted in a quorum, the right to participate in the proceedings of the board and to vote on any and all matters. The director so designating such a deputy or assistant director shall be responsible for the acts of the person acting under such designation in the same manner and to the same extent that the director is responsible for the acts of the deputy or assistant director performing his official duties as deputy or assistant director of the department.
-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:35 | 7.9. (a) Notwithstanding any provision of law to the contrary, the Controller, the Treasurer, the Director of Finance, or the Superintendent of Public Instruction may designate any deputy of his or her office to act in his or her place and stead on any state board, commission, committee, or governing board of a state agency with respect to the exercise of statutory powers and duties of any of those bodies. The deputy, while sitting on a board, commission, committee, or governing board of a state agency may exercise the same powers that the Controller, the Treasurer, the Director of Finance, or the Superintendent of Public Instruction may exercise as if he or she were personally present. The Controller, the Treasurer, the Director of Finance, or the Superintendent of Public Instruction so designating a deputy shall be responsible for the acts of the deputy acting under the designation in the same manner and to the same extent that the Controller, the Treasurer, the Director of Finance, or the Superintendent of Public Instruction is responsible for the acts of the deputy performing his or her official duties as deputy to the Controller, the Treasurer, the Director of Finance, or the Superintendent of Public Instruction.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.5, § 7.6(a), § 7.8, § 7.9(a) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:22, src:GOV-ss-1-26:24, src:GOV-ss-1-26:33, src:GOV-ss-1-26:35)
-- Each says the officer "shall be responsible for the acts of the deputy acting under such designation in the same manner and to the same extent that the officer is
-- responsible for the acts of the deputy performing his or her official duties as" deputy.  How far that is, the deposit does not say; the function compares.
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision that designates a deputy`
      `the deputy acted under the designation` IS A BOOLEAN
      extent IS AN `Extent of an officer's responsibility`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the officer is responsible for the act of the deputy` provision `the deputy acted under the designation` extent MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF provision EQUALS `another provision`
            THEN REFUSE "Gov. Code §§ 7.5, 7.6(a), 7.8 and 7.9(a) make the officer responsible for the acts of a deputy designated under them; no other provision is deposited that does"
        IF NOT `the deputy acted under the designation`
            THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE extent EQUALS `the same extent as for the deputy's official duties in the deputy's own post`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:22 | 7.5. Whenever, by any law, the director of any state department is made a member of a state board, commission, or committee, or of the governing body of any state agency or authority, the director may designate a deputy director of that department holding a position specified in subdivision (f) or (g) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution to act as such member in his or her place and stead, to all intents and purposes as though the director were personally present, including the right of the deputy to be counted in constituting a quorum, to participate in the proceedings of the board, commission, committee, or other governing body, and to vote upon any and all matters. Not more than one director shall be represented by such a deputy at any meeting or session of a board, commission, committee, or other governing body. The director so designating such a deputy shall be responsible for the acts of the deputy acting under such designation in the same manner and to the same extent that the director is responsible for the acts of the deputy performing his or her official duties as deputy director of the department.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.5 (src:GOV-ss-1-26:22)
-- "Not more than one director shall be represented by such a deputy at any meeting or session of a board, commission, committee, or other governing body."
-- § 7.8 lifts this for the State Allocation Board, for the three Directors it names (fork F-7.8); a meeting of another body under § 7.8 is not answered.
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision that designates a deputy`
      body IS A `Body at whose meeting a deputy acts`
      `the number of directors represented by such deputies at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`this many directors may be represented by deputies at a meeting under` provision body `the number of directors represented by such deputies at the meeting` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF provision EQUALS `Section 7.5`
            THEN `the number of directors represented by such deputies at the meeting` LESS THAN 2
        IF provision EQUALS `Section 7.8` AND body EQUALS `the State Allocation Board`
            THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE REFUSE "Gov. Code § 7.5 limits the directors represented at a meeting to one and § 7.8 lifts the limit for the State Allocation Board; the deposit does not say what limit applies under another provision or at another body"

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:33 | 7.8. Notwithstanding anything in this code to the contrary, the Directors of Finance, General Services, and Education may appoint any deputy or assistant director in their respective departments to act in their place and stead on the State Allocation Board, irrespective of whether said deputy or assistant director holds a position specified in subdivision (g) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution, and irrespective of whether there shall be more than one such person representing a director at any meeting of such board. Such person, while sitting on said board, shall have all the powers the director he represents would have had, including the right to be counted in a quorum, the right to participate in the proceedings of the board and to vote on any and all matters. The director so designating such a deputy or assistant director shall be responsible for the acts of the person acting under such designation in the same manner and to the same extent that the director is responsible for the acts of the deputy or assistant director performing his official duties as deputy or assistant director of the department.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.8 (src:GOV-ss-1-26:33)
GIVEN `the number of persons representing the same director at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`more persons may represent the same director at a meeting under Section 7.8` `the number of persons representing the same director at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the number of persons representing the same director at the meeting` LESS THAN 2
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Gov. Code § 7.8 says the appointment is irrespective of whether there is more than one such person representing a director at any meeting; the deposit does not say whether that means several persons for one director (fork F-7.8)"

§ `Gov. Code § 7.6: officers whose offices the Constitution creates`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:24 | 7.6. (a) If by law, any officer whose office is created by the California Constitution is made a member of a state board, commission, or committee, or of the governing body of any state agency or authority, the officer may designate a deputy of his or her office holding a position specified in subdivision (c) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution to act as the member in the constitutional officer’s place and stead, to all intents and purposes as though the constitutional officer was personally present, including the right of the deputy to be counted in constituting a quorum, to participate in the proceedings of the board, commission, committee, or other governing body, and to vote upon any and all matters. The constitutional officer so designating a deputy shall be responsible for the acts of the deputy acting under the designation in the same manner and to the same extent that the constitutional officer is responsible for the acts of the deputy performing his or her official duties as a deputy of the office of the constitutional officer.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.6(a) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:24)
GIVEN `the officer holds an office created by the California Constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is by law a member of a state board, commission, or committee, or of the governing body of a state agency or authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a deputy of the officer's office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds a position specified in subdivision (c) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Gov. Code § 7.6(a) lets the officer designate` `the officer holds an office created by the California Constitution` `the officer is by law a member of a state board, commission, or committee, or of the governing body of a state agency or authority` `the person is a deputy of the officer's office` `the person holds a position specified in subdivision (c) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution` MEANS
        `the officer holds an office created by the California Constitution`
    AND `the officer is by law a member of a state board, commission, or committee, or of the governing body of a state agency or authority`
    AND `the person is a deputy of the officer's office`
    AND `the person holds a position specified in subdivision (c) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:25 | (b) The Lieutenant Governor may designate any person in his or her office holding a position specified in subdivision (c) or (f) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution to act as a deputy for the purposes of this section only. However, the Lieutenant Governor may not appoint a person to act as a deputy for him or her at meetings of the Senate, or of the Regents of the University of California, or of the Trustees of the California State University.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.6(b) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:25)
GIVEN `the person is in the Lieutenant Governor's office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds a position specified in subdivision (c) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds a position specified in subdivision (f) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Gov. Code § 7.6(b) lets the Lieutenant Governor designate` `the person is in the Lieutenant Governor's office` `the person holds a position specified in subdivision (c) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution` `the person holds a position specified in subdivision (f) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution` MEANS
        `the person is in the Lieutenant Governor's office`
    AND (   `the person holds a position specified in subdivision (c) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution`
         OR `the person holds a position specified in subdivision (f) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution`)

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:25 | (b) The Lieutenant Governor may designate any person in his or her office holding a position specified in subdivision (c) or (f) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution to act as a deputy for the purposes of this section only. However, the Lieutenant Governor may not appoint a person to act as a deputy for him or her at meetings of the Senate, or of the Regents of the University of California, or of the Trustees of the California State University.
-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:28 | (e) The Superintendent of Public Instruction may designate any person in his or her office holding a position specified in Section 2.1 of Article IX of the California Constitution to act as a deputy for the purposes of this section. However, the Superintendent of Public Instruction may not appoint a person to act as a deputy for him or her at meetings of the State Board of Education, of the Regents of the University of California, or of the Trustees of the California State University.
-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:37 | (c) The Superintendent of Public Instruction may not appoint a person pursuant to subdivision (a) to act as a deputy for him or her at meetings of the State Board of Education, the Regents of the University of California, or the Trustees of the California State University.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.6(b), § 7.6(e), § 7.9(c) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:25, src:GOV-ss-1-26:28, src:GOV-ss-1-26:37)
-- The Lieutenant Governor "may not appoint a person to act as a deputy for him or her at meetings of the Senate, or of the Regents of the University of California, or of the
-- Trustees of the California State University"; the Superintendent of Public Instruction may not at meetings of the State Board of Education, the Regents or the Trustees.
-- For any other office the text names, these sentences forbid nothing.
GIVEN officer IS AN `Office the text names`
      body IS A `Body at whose meeting a deputy acts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a deputy may not be appointed to act for the officer at meetings of` officer body MEANS
    CONSIDER officer
    WHEN `the Lieutenant Governor`
        THEN    body EQUALS `the Senate`
             OR body EQUALS `the Regents of the University of California`
             OR body EQUALS `the Trustees of the California State University`
    WHEN `the Superintendent of Public Instruction`
        THEN    body EQUALS `the State Board of Education`
             OR body EQUALS `the Regents of the University of California`
             OR body EQUALS `the Trustees of the California State University`
    WHEN `the Chief Justice of the California Supreme Court` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Attorney General` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Controller` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Treasurer` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Director of Finance` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Director of General Services` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Director of Education` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an office the text does not name` THEN FALSE

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:26 | (c) The Chief Justice of the California Supreme Court may designate a judge or employee of a state court or an employee of the Administrative Office of the Courts to act as a deputy for the purposes of this section.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.6(c) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:26)
GIVEN `the person is a judge or employee of a state court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an employee of the Administrative Office of the Courts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Gov. Code § 7.6(c) lets the Chief Justice designate` `the person is a judge or employee of a state court` `the person is an employee of the Administrative Office of the Courts` MEANS
       `the person is a judge or employee of a state court`
    OR `the person is an employee of the Administrative Office of the Courts`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:27 | (d) The Attorney General may also designate any employee in his or her office to act as a deputy for the purpose of this section. However, no person designated by the Attorney General pursuant to this section to act as a member on any state board, commission, committee, or governing body of which the Attorney General is presiding officer shall act as presiding officer in his or her place.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.6(d) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:27)
GIVEN `the person is an employee in the Attorney General's office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Gov. Code § 7.6(d) lets the Attorney General designate` `the person is an employee in the Attorney General's office` MEANS
    `the person is an employee in the Attorney General's office`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:27 | (d) The Attorney General may also designate any employee in his or her office to act as a deputy for the purpose of this section. However, no person designated by the Attorney General pursuant to this section to act as a member on any state board, commission, committee, or governing body of which the Attorney General is presiding officer shall act as presiding officer in his or her place.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.6(d) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:27)
-- "no person designated by the Attorney General ... to act as a member on any state board, commission, committee, or governing body of which the Attorney General is
-- presiding officer shall act as presiding officer in his or her place."  A body of which the Attorney General is not presiding officer is not spoken of.
GIVEN `the Attorney General is the presiding officer of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person designated by the Attorney General may act as presiding officer in the Attorney General's place` `the Attorney General is the presiding officer of the body` MEANS
    IF `the Attorney General is the presiding officer of the body`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE REFUSE "Gov. Code § 7.6(d) forbids the Attorney General's designee to preside only on a body of which the Attorney General is presiding officer"

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:28 | (e) The Superintendent of Public Instruction may designate any person in his or her office holding a position specified in Section 2.1 of Article IX of the California Constitution to act as a deputy for the purposes of this section. However, the Superintendent of Public Instruction may not appoint a person to act as a deputy for him or her at meetings of the State Board of Education, of the Regents of the University of California, or of the Trustees of the California State University.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.6(e) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:28)
GIVEN `the person is in the office of the Superintendent of Public Instruction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds a position specified in Section 2.1 of Article IX of the California Constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Gov. Code § 7.6(e) lets the Superintendent of Public Instruction designate` `the person is in the office of the Superintendent of Public Instruction` `the person holds a position specified in Section 2.1 of Article IX of the California Constitution` MEANS
        `the person is in the office of the Superintendent of Public Instruction`
    AND `the person holds a position specified in Section 2.1 of Article IX of the California Constitution`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:29 | (f) Notwithstanding subdivisions (a) to (e), inclusive, not more than one officer subject to this section shall be represented by a deputy subject to this section at any meeting or session of the State Lands Commission.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.6(f) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:29)
-- Fork F-7.6f: the officers counted are those subject to § 7.6 and the deputies those subject to § 7.6 (see the head of this file).
GIVEN `the number of officers subject to Section 7.6 represented by a deputy subject to Section 7.6 at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`this many officers may be represented at a meeting of the State Lands Commission under Section 7.6` `the number of officers subject to Section 7.6 represented by a deputy subject to Section 7.6 at the meeting` MEANS
    `the number of officers subject to Section 7.6 represented by a deputy subject to Section 7.6 at the meeting` LESS THAN 2

§ `Gov. Code § 7.7: saving of Section 7`

DECLARE `Section the saving clause speaks of` IS ONE OF
    `Section 7.5`
    `Section 7.6`
    `another section`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:31 | 7.7. The provisions of Sections 7.5 and 7.6 do not affect or modify in any manner the provisions of Section 7.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.7 (src:GOV-ss-1-26:31)
GIVEN section IS A `Section the saving clause speaks of`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section affects or modifies Section 7` section MEANS
    CONSIDER section
    WHEN `Section 7.5` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Section 7.6` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `another section` THEN REFUSE "Gov. Code § 7.7 says that Sections 7.5 and 7.6 do not affect or modify Section 7; it says nothing of another section"

§ `Gov. Code § 7.8: the State Allocation Board`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:33 | 7.8. Notwithstanding anything in this code to the contrary, the Directors of Finance, General Services, and Education may appoint any deputy or assistant director in their respective departments to act in their place and stead on the State Allocation Board, irrespective of whether said deputy or assistant director holds a position specified in subdivision (g) of Section 4 of Article VII of the California Constitution, and irrespective of whether there shall be more than one such person representing a director at any meeting of such board. Such person, while sitting on said board, shall have all the powers the director he represents would have had, including the right to be counted in a quorum, the right to participate in the proceedings of the board and to vote on any and all matters. The director so designating such a deputy or assistant director shall be responsible for the acts of the person acting under such designation in the same manner and to the same extent that the director is responsible for the acts of the deputy or assistant director performing his official duties as deputy or assistant director of the department.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.8 (src:GOV-ss-1-26:33)
GIVEN director IS AN `Office the text names`
      body IS A `Body at whose meeting a deputy acts`
      `the person is a deputy or assistant director in the director's department` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Gov. Code § 7.8 lets the director designate` director body `the person is a deputy or assistant director in the director's department` MEANS
        (   director EQUALS `the Director of Finance`
         OR director EQUALS `the Director of General Services`
         OR director EQUALS `the Director of Education`)
    AND body EQUALS `the State Allocation Board`
    AND `the person is a deputy or assistant director in the director's department`

§ `Gov. Code § 7.9 and § 7.9a: the Controller, the Treasurer, the Director of Finance and the Superintendent of Public Instruction`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:35 | 7.9. (a) Notwithstanding any provision of law to the contrary, the Controller, the Treasurer, the Director of Finance, or the Superintendent of Public Instruction may designate any deputy of his or her office to act in his or her place and stead on any state board, commission, committee, or governing board of a state agency with respect to the exercise of statutory powers and duties of any of those bodies. The deputy, while sitting on a board, commission, committee, or governing board of a state agency may exercise the same powers that the Controller, the Treasurer, the Director of Finance, or the Superintendent of Public Instruction may exercise as if he or she were personally present. The Controller, the Treasurer, the Director of Finance, or the Superintendent of Public Instruction so designating a deputy shall be responsible for the acts of the deputy acting under the designation in the same manner and to the same extent that the Controller, the Treasurer, the Director of Finance, or the Superintendent of Public Instruction is responsible for the acts of the deputy performing his or her official duties as deputy to the Controller, the Treasurer, the Director of Finance, or the Superintendent of Public Instruction.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.9(a) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:35)
GIVEN officer IS AN `Office the text names`
      `the person is a deputy of the officer's office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a state board, commission, committee, or governing board of a state agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Gov. Code § 7.9(a) lets the officer designate` officer `the person is a deputy of the officer's office` `the body is a state board, commission, committee, or governing board of a state agency` MEANS
        (   officer EQUALS `the Controller`
         OR officer EQUALS `the Treasurer`
         OR officer EQUALS `the Director of Finance`
         OR officer EQUALS `the Superintendent of Public Instruction`)
    AND `the person is a deputy of the officer's office`
    AND `the body is a state board, commission, committee, or governing board of a state agency`

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:36 | (b) At the request of the Controller or the Treasurer, two employees of each officer, who hold permanent civil service status and have been designated deputies under this section, shall be classified and compensated as career executives at category level IV or category level V.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.9(b) (src:GOV-ss-1-26:36)
-- "At the request of the Controller or the Treasurer, two employees of each officer, who hold permanent civil service status and have been designated deputies under
-- this section, shall be classified and compensated as career executives at category level IV or category level V."  The text names two employees; it does not say what
-- follows when fewer than two employees qualify, or which two when more do.  The function says whether the duty arises, and refuses where the text leaves it open.
GIVEN officer IS AN `Office the text names`
      `the officer has requested it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of the officer's employees who hold permanent civil service status and have been designated deputies under Section 7.9` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Gov. Code § 7.9(b) requires two employees of the officer to be classified as career executives` officer `the officer has requested it` `the number of the officer's employees who hold permanent civil service status and have been designated deputies under Section 7.9` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (officer EQUALS `the Controller` OR officer EQUALS `the Treasurer`) THEN FALSE
        IF NOT `the officer has requested it` THEN FALSE
        IF `the number of the officer's employees who hold permanent civil service status and have been designated deputies under Section 7.9` LESS THAN 2
            THEN REFUSE "Gov. Code § 7.9(b) speaks of two employees of each officer; it does not say what follows when fewer than two hold permanent civil service status and have been designated deputies"
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:36 | (b) At the request of the Controller or the Treasurer, two employees of each officer, who hold permanent civil service status and have been designated deputies under this section, shall be classified and compensated as career executives at category level IV or category level V.
-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:39 | 7.9a. At the request of the Controller, two employees of that officer, in addition to those provided for in Section 7.9, shall be classified and compensated as career executives at category level IV or category level V.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.9(b), § 7.9a (src:GOV-ss-1-26:36, src:GOV-ss-1-26:39)
-- Category level IV or category level V; the text does not choose between them.
GIVEN level IS A `Category level of a career executive`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the career executive may be classified at` level MEANS
    NOT (level EQUALS `another category level`)

-- src:GOV-ss-1-26:39 | 7.9a. At the request of the Controller, two employees of that officer, in addition to those provided for in Section 7.9, shall be classified and compensated as career executives at category level IV or category level V.
@ref Gov. Code § 7.9a (src:GOV-ss-1-26:39)
-- "At the request of the Controller, two employees of that officer, in addition to those provided for in Section 7.9, shall be classified and compensated as career
-- executives at category level IV or category level V."  Unlike § 7.9(b), the text does not require these employees to hold permanent civil service status or to be deputies.
GIVEN officer IS AN `Office the text names`
      `the officer has requested it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Gov. Code § 7.9a requires two more employees of the officer to be classified as career executives` officer `the officer has requested it` MEANS
    officer EQUALS `the Controller` AND `the officer has requested it`
